20
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:33,040
 It's primarily an issuer-focused regulatory regime that establishes criteria that issuers

21
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:36,760
 of stable coins have to meet in order to be compliant with the law.

22
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:41,480
 That's really important because obviously stable coins are supposed to represent a dollar.

23
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:45,840
 It's important to make sure that in particular the underlying collateral that backs those

24
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:49,360
 assets actually means that those assets are worth a dollar.

25
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:53,000
 The crypto industry has a long history of experimenting with these types of things and

26
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,120
 there are instances where the collateral backing stable coins has turned out not to be there.

27
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:02,040
