28
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:08,680
 People might remember the Terra Luna debacle where the stable coin broke the peg and cratered

29
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:10,600
 and left a lot of people in the lurch.

30
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:15,400
 So this bill you're saying is designed to prevent things like that from happening again.

31
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,400
 That's exactly right.

32
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:21,320
 It gives regulatory clarity, establishes clear thresholds around collateral requirements,

33
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:23,360
 requires assets to be backed one to one.

34
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:25,920
 So something like Terra Luna doesn't happen again.

35
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:30,400
 That trust is really important in establishing that stable coins function as dollars.

36
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:35,280
 When you hold a dollar that you take out of a Bank of America ATM or a city bank ATM,

37
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,320
